WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
You already paid to make the phone ring.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.000
But when you are working, you cannot always answer.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.500
In a controlled pilot, TradeCatch texts back within seconds,
under your company's name.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.000
The customer stays engaged instead of calling your competitor.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.750
It collects the customer's name, problem, urgency, address,
and a photo while you stay on the job.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:28.000
When you check your phone, the lead is already qualified.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.500
The right technician receives one clear job summary.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.000
They can accept, decline, or call;
a backup can be alerted if no one responds.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Acceptance notifies the customer.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Entitled, linked Growth pilot organizations book
in-app—without native Google or Outlook sync.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Starter pilots can follow up on quotes on days 1, 3, 7, and 14.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.000
A reply stops the sequence; the pipeline is only for entitled,
linked Growth pilot organizations.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.500
Figures are illustrative, not promised results.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:07.000
Workspaces show linked-organization data only—not
self-serve SaaS or native two-way CRM.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Stop losing jobs when you cannot answer.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Get your free missed-opportunity audit with TradeCatch.
